From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: feder-cr <85809106+feder-cr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:19:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(naga spv-out): Pass external texture globals to functions
 correctly

When a `texture_external` global is passed to a function, the call site
loaded the parameters buffer through an `OpAccessChain` typed with the
regular `NagaExternalTextureParams` struct, but the uniform variable holds
the std140-compatible struct (its `mat3x2` members are split into
columns), so the module was invalid. The function prelude already loads
the std140 value and converts it to the regular type; pass that value.

That conversion function was only registered when some function sampled,
loaded or queried an external texture, so a module that only forwarded an
external texture global panicked when writing the prelude. Register it
whenever a function uses an external texture global.
---
